        "original_id": "2a0a4562-115c-532d-865b-d8d31109d39f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Pacific Films, Pacific Film Unit, Pacific Film Productions Ltd\n- People: Alun Falconer, Roger Mirams, John O'Shea\n- Places: Wellington, New Zealand, China\n- Roles: ex-National Film Unit staff, defender, vice-captain\n- Organizations: National Film Unit, Sunderland, Republic of Ireland national team\n\nFacts:\n- The Pacific Film Unit was established in Wellington, New Zealand, in 1948 by ex-National Film Unit staff Alun Falconer and Roger Mirams.\n- In 1950, John O'Shea joined Pacific Film Unit.\n- In 1950, Alun Falconer left Pacific Film Unit to pursue a career in China.\n- In 1950, the company Pacific Film Unit changed its name to Pacific Film Productions Ltd.\n- John Francis O'Shea was born on 30 April 1981.\n- John Francis O'Shea is an Irish footballer.\n- John Francis O'Shea plays as a defender for Sunderland.\n- John Francis O'Shea plays for the Republic of Ireland national team and serves as its vice-captain.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
